@startuml access-reach
!include _theme.iuml
left to right direction

actor "Person" as Person
rectangle "Repository" as Repo

package "Declared by the organisation" {
  rectangle "organization.members.base_permission\nA floor under every repository" as Base
  rectangle "organization.roles.<name>\nAssignment only" as Role
  rectangle "organization.teams.<slug>.membership\nWho is on the team" as Team
}

package "Declared by the repository" {
  rectangle "access.teams.<slug>\nWhat the team may do here" as TeamGrant
  rectangle "access.users.<login>\nA direct collaborator" as Direct
}

Person --> Base : as any member
Person --> Team : as member or maintainer
Person --> Role : as a holder
Person --> Direct : by name

Base --> Repo : every repository the\norganisation owns
Team --> TeamGrant
TeamGrant --> Repo : one repository
Direct --> Repo : one repository
Role --> Repo : every repository the\norganisation owns

note bottom of Base
  <b>The floor is not a grant.</b> No repository
  policy can go below it, so lowering it takes
  access away from people no policy names.
  Reported as <b>sensitive</b>.
end note

note bottom of Direct
  Revocation is spelled <b>none</b>. Deleting the
  line stops managing the grant; it does not
  remove it.
end note
@enduml
